title: The January Uprising
subtitle: Berlin's workers are in the streets.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 1
max-visits: 1

= The January Uprising

On 4 January the government dismissed Emil Eichhorn, the left-wing police chief of Berlin. The next day hundreds of thousands of workers marched in protest. Armed men occupied the newspaper district, and a Revolutionary Committee, with Karl Liebknecht among its members, declared the Ebert government deposed.

The Zentrale was not consulted. Luxemburg thinks the uprising is premature; the Berlin district, which follows the ultra-left, is already on the barricades. Noske is gathering the Freikorps outside the city.

- @overthrow: Back the Revolutionary Committee and try to overthrow Ebert.
- @occupations: Defend the occupations, but refuse an armed insurrection.
- @negotiate: Call for negotiations and a withdrawal from the buildings.

@overthrow
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs 10 Unity. ?] Thrills the radicals. The Freikorps will not forgive it.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_name +] line forbids an uprising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.militancy += 20;
Q.repression += 25;
Q.stability -= 5;
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 15;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 15;
Q.district_berlin_members -= 0.5;
Q.district_berlin_loyalty += 15;
Q.spd_relation -= 10;
Q.leaders_risk = 60;
!}

The party throws itself into the fight. For a few days, the government's fate seems uncertain.

- @hunt: Continue...

@occupations
subtitle: The middle course. Berlin is disappointed, and the Freikorps come anyway.
on-arrival: militancy += 8; repression += 15; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 5; district_berlin_loyalty -= 5; spd_relation -= 5; leaders_risk = 40

The party defends the occupied buildings, but refuses to call for the government's overthrow.

- @hunt: Continue...

@negotiate
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs 10 Unity. ?] Avoids a massacre, perhaps. Berlin's workers will call it betrayal.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_name +] line forbids negotiating with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.militancy -= 5;
Q.repression += 5;
Q.uspd_relation += 10;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 20;
